# Normalise to LF in the repository and ON CHECKOUT, on every platform.
#
# `text=auto` alone is not enough here. It normalises what gets STORED, but a judge
# on Windows with Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` still gets CRLF in
# their working tree — and `forge fmt --check`, which `npm run gate` runs, then flags
# 16 files and the whole gate exits 1. That reads as "this project is broken" when the
# only thing wrong is a line ending. `eol=lf` pins the checkout too, so the gate gives
# the same answer on Linux, macOS and Windows.
#
# Measured 2026-09-07: this machine has `core.autocrlf=true` and the repo had no
# .gitattributes, so the Windows-judge path was a real failure, not a hypothetical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
